<title>TURKEY: Turkish Brisa Q1 profits rise 51 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Brisa Q1 profits rise 51 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 2,029.22 vs   1,344.31</p>
<p>    Net profit		  2,157.31 vs   1,429.17</p>
<p>    Net sales		   8,062.00 vs   4,884.72</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  2,730.88 vs   1,751.15</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,372.36 vs     572.48</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 422.87 vs     153.20</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   1.29 vs	17.95</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense     304.90 vs     199.11</p>
<p>    Total debts		 9,143.51 vs   6,608.96</p>
<p>    Equity		     15,879.72 vs   8,560.47</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,063.13 vs   1,063.13</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish tyre maker Brisa Bridgestone Sabanci Lastik Sanayi ve Ticaret A.S. is jointly owned by Japan's Bridgestone Corp and Turkish industrial Sabanci group.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
